{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03S2", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'E", "MATH_0001": "$j_!\\mathcal{F} \\to j_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{etale-lemma-finite-etale-etale-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0595ed9d5da10f4c01ba94a203c14c969c02d173db94c6dc493b87edd1b02ce8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e8327c7db7ccc94b6d803518690e05f2ce7424c8fb6e30acfd461dd47cbe8919", "source_text": "It suffices to check <MATH_0001>\nis an isomorphism <ACCENT_0001>tale locally on <MATH_0002>.\nThus we may assume <MATH_0003> is a finite disjoint union\nof isomorphisms, see\n<ACCENT_0002>tale Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe omit the proof in this case.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:739940b7d3d3690d4a893e6751d6389f15c88374a58bd6da5657b01c7be5f729", "unit_id": "tag:03S7:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03S2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Z \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$j : U \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n0 \\to j_!j^{-1}\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F} \\to i_*i^{-1}\\mathcal{F} \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$X_\\etale$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-ses-associated-to-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ae1fe5c9b2eebdcfb414f9f663f1ad50a2e1f899ff2fcd33aae2920153f70fca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a1c1f9a7b40e612c093a9d23bb85e596e8c8f5ea5482289ab78d2b810e06c40", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a closed subscheme and let\n<MATH_0003> be the complement. Denote <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>\nthe inclusion morphisms. For every abelian sheaf <MATH_0006> on <MATH_0007>\nthere is a canonical short exact sequence\n<MATH_0008>\non <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9dc07b8ebf2bc593f010d312732205fc42a9448b7b80888aa9b07162687f778f", "unit_id": "tag:095L:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03S2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\overline{x}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\overline{x} \\in U$", "MATH_0004": "$i_*i^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\overline{x} \\in Z$", "MATH_0006": "$j_!j^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-stalk-pushforward-closed-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{proposition-describe-jshriek}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ff1762e2a2f864dc2aefe86bbfab903ba593d3650efa535e7fbb2e9e4796a876", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d98f094a6c8a4918e818187f56c1c76750f0825c88c1435ea4f2dc18262799c", "source_text": "We obtain the maps by the adjointness properties of the functors\ninvolved. For a geometric point <MATH_0001> in <MATH_0002> we have either\n<MATH_0003> in which case the map on the left hand side\nis an isomorphism on stalks and the stalk of <MATH_0004>\nis zero or <MATH_0005> in which case the map on the right hand side\nis an isomorphism on stalks and the stalk of <MATH_0006>\nis zero. Here we have used the description of stalks of\nLemma <REF_0001> and\nProposition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0d2777276fd00391391252ed0cbf2c5c8d59e13f7ecdfc4b3f94522f1f3eeab4", "unit_id": "tag:095L:proof"}
